{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","max_tokens":768,"stream":true,"system":"Keep the answer short.","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"Find the unique integer selector from 1 through 99 that has remainder 2 when divided by 5, remainder 0 when divided by 7, and remainder 7 when divided by 11. Work out the constraints before answering. State the selector with a short explanation."},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Selector: 7**\n\n- Remainder 0 mod 7 means x is a multiple of 7: 7, 14, 21, …\n- Remainder 2 mod 5 means x ends in 2 or 7. Among multiples of 7 below 100, that leaves 7, 42, 77.\n- Remainder 7 mod 11: 7 gives 7 ✓, 42 gives 9 ✗, 77 gives 0 ✗.\n\nSo x = 7. The moduli 5, 7, 11 are pairwise coprime, so solutions repeat only every 385. That makes 7 the only solution in 1–99."}]},{"role":"user","content":"Now reply exactly OK."}],"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"output_config":{"effort":"max"}}